      "role": "user",
      "content": "thanks for that. some of the people at my meeting are saying that density is basically the only way to actually solve the housing crisis and that staying with single-family zoning is just a way for people to block progress. do you think that's a fair assessment or is there more to it than just \"blocking progress\"?",
